      "body": "concept ACK\r\n\r\nmakes sense to update `m_keep_alive` in the same critical section as the send\r\nbuffer, since both are read together under the same lock (`m_send_mutex`). this\r\nkeeps the related state changes in sync and does not allow the I/O thread to\r\nview an inconsistent state while the next response is being queued\r\n\r\n---\r\n**edit**: the motivation is fine but since this scenario is not easy to reach _pragmatically_,\r\ni'd rather delay review",
